%[text] %[text:anchor:T_F617CF66] # Statics: Forces in Equilibrium Solutions
%[text] [⇦ Main Menu](file:MainMenu.m)
%[text] In a variety of engineering disciplines and in physics, you may want to analyze static systems. This requires drawing a force diagram (vectors!) indicating all of the components that must balance to keep a static system from becoming a dynamic system. Adding up all of the vectors in the system must result in the zero vector in any static system. 
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] **Before you get started:**
%[text] This live script is intended to be used with the code visible and output inline. On the **View** tab of the MATLAB Toolstrip, in the **View** section, select **Output Inline**. Alternately, select **Output inline** using the icon ![live script output inline icon](text:image:323f) at the top right of the Live Editor pane.
